    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0512" n="426" xml:id="pg426"/>

                <head>No. 189.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"><persName corresp="#p_SET1" type="from"
                            >Sir Edward Thornton</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-06-19"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 19, 1873</date>.
                        (Received June 19.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer you to a note
                    addressed to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_JBD1">Bancroft Davis</persName> by Mr.
                    Pakenham on the 10th of September, 1871, asking the consideration by the
                    Government of the United States of a proposal made by the government of
                    Newfoundland that American fishermen should be admitted to the right of taking
                    seals within the territorial jurisdiction of Newfoundland on the condition of
                    the admission of the produce of the Newfoundland seal-fishery into the United
                    States free of duty.</p>
                <p>Mr. <persName corresp="#p_JBD1">Bancroft Davis</persName> replied, on the 23d of
                    the same month, that the subject would receive consideration, but that the
                    proposal was one which needed congressional approval before it could be
                    definitively accepted by the Department of State.</p>
                <p>In compliance with an instruction which I have received this morning from Earl
                    Granville, I have the honor to inquire whether any steps have been taken by your
                    Department with a view to carry out the proposal made by the government of
                    Newfoundland, with regard to which Mr. <persName corresp="#p_JBD1">Bancroft
                        Davis</persName> was at the time informed that Her Majesty’s government
                    would be glad if it could be acceded to.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_SET1">EDW’D THORNTON</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
